● [mI read the intent for play 009 and both context documents. The play fits the vision. Tapping a stop to see how far away its buses are is still glanceable, involves no planning,  
  and saves nothing, so it doesn't touch any non-goal. The tech stack doesn't need to change: this is UI and domain logic in the existing React/MapLibre app.[K
[K
  One gap: the vision only describes the app showing [1myour nearest[22m stop, based on location. This play adds choosing any stop by hand, which is a new capability, so I think the      
  vision should say so. I'd make two small wording changes to [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/vision.md[m:[K
[K
  - [1mVision:[22m "…showing where you are, your nearest Metrobus stop (or any stop you tap), the live position of every Metrobus bus, and how many minutes each approaching bus is from   
    that stop."[K
  - [1mLocation-aware principle:[22m "Use the device's location to find the nearest stop automatically. The user can tap any other stop to look at it instead; tapping away goes back to   
    the nearest one."[K
[K
  Nothing else would change, and a tapped stop stays temporary (it isn't saved as a favourite).[K
[K
  Can I make these two edits to the vision?[K
